rem Circle of Coins
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=728

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Limit integer = 10 ** 7
arg Prime integer = 1000000007

rem With g = gcd(n, k): F = 2^(n-g+1) if
rem v2(k) <= v2(n), else 2^(n-g). Write
rem n = t h, k = t r with r, h coprime.
rem For h > 1 the residues r give
rem 2 phi(h) 2^(t(h-1)) when h is even
rem and 3 phi(h) / 2 2^(t(h-1)) when
rem odd. The geometric sum over t up to
rem N // h is taken in closed form; the
rem case k = n adds 2 N.
Phi = (0 to Limit) copy
for P in primes to Limit
  Slice = P to Limit by P
  Old = Phi Slice
  Phi Slice = Old - Old // P
end
Heights = 2 to Limit
Coeff = Phi (2 to Limit)
Even = ((Heights mod 2) equal 0) integer
EvenPart = Even * 2 * Coeff
OddPart = (1 - Even) * 3 * Coeff // 2
Coeff = EvenPart + OddPart
Base = 2 (Heights - 1) Prime powmod
Counts = Limit // Heights
Powers = Base Counts Prime powmod
Less = Base - 1
Power = Prime - 2
Inverse = Less Power Prime powmod
Raised = Base * (Powers - 1) mod Prime
Geometric = Raised * Inverse mod Prime
Reduced = Coeff mod Prime
Terms = Reduced * Geometric mod Prime
Total = Terms sum
return (2 * Limit + Total) mod Prime
